.git
docs
**/node_modules
**/vendor
**/.venv
**/venv
# Any real .env, anywhere in the tree -- not just backend/.env. This is what
# keeps a developer's own langchain_runner/.env (which per backend/.env.example
# is where the workflow editor writes the user's actual provider keys) out of
# the image. .env.example files are templates with no real values, so they're
# let back through -- the entrypoint needs backend/.env.example to render
# backend/.env at boot.
**/.env
!**/.env.example
frontend/assets/js/config.js
frontend/voice/config.json
**/__pycache__
.scratch_parity
# Logs anywhere in the tree (e.g. backend_typescript/logs/backend.log, which
# Logger.ts mirrors all console output to) and any .env backup files.
**/*.log
**/logs/
**/*.bak*
.claude
.superpowers
